<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  OpenSVN deliberately requests no hardened-runtime exceptions.

	  The two things that usually force an entitlement here do not apply:

	  1. The app is not sandboxed (ADR-0003). It has to reach working copies
	     the user picks anywhere on disk, and a sandbox would turn every
	     checkout into a security-scoped bookmark problem without adding
	     protection to a tool whose job is running svn on user files.

	  2. It launches a child process rather than loading third-party code into
	     its own address space. The bundled svn and svnadmin are signed by the
	     same identity as the app, and they load their own dylibs from
	     Contents/Resources/svn/lib — library validation is satisfied because
	     those are our signatures too. No disable-library-validation, no
	     allow-unsigned-executable-memory, no allow-dyld-environment-variables.

	  Keeping the file empty and explicit means that if this ever changes, the
	  change lands in review as a diff to a security-relevant file instead of
	  as a flag on a build command line.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
